<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valence</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Valence, Drôme</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valence is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>, and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drome">Drôme</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. Founded as the Roman colony of Valentia in the territory of the Segovellauni, it became a bishopric and the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinois">Valentinois</a>, held by the counts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> family. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vi">Pope Pius VI</a> died there in exile in 1799.</p></div>
